  "aiContextParagraph": "The incident at Seattle-Tacoma International Airport involved the detention of two passengers by Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) agents as they attempted to board a flight. Video footage of the event circulated widely, drawing criticism from various public figures, including the Governor of Washington, who described the actions as out of control. Labor unions have joined in the critique of the agency's conduct, while reports from individuals present during the detention, including family members of those arrested, claimed that the subjects were subjected to physical force during the encounter. The arrests have prompted protests and a broader discussion regarding the methods employed by federal agents during immigration enforcement operations within airport terminals. The situation remains a subject of ongoing scrutiny from local government officials and the public regarding the use of authority in transit environments.",
